# The one place a family version is written. Every tree's manifest, toolchain
# pin, version catalog and Swift manifests must agree with this file;
# scripts/check-pins.sh fails on the first one that does not. A family release
# is one commit: edit this file, re-pin the trees, re-record where the release
# notes say bytes moved, open one pull request.
DUET=0.7.0
DUET_SERVICES=0.11.1
DUET_TOOLS=0.24.0
MOCKS_BUNDLE=0.6.2
KSP_MOCKS=0.2.1
# The Swift-first track (the tutorial*-swift-* and tutorial*-twins-* trees)
# pins its own duet-tools release and mocks bundle: its twin trees need the
# twins support duet-tools 0.34.0 carries, whose mocks floor is 0.7.0. Every
# tree of the track carries the same two pins, so a rung differs from the one
# before it by its exercise stub alone.
DUET_TOOLS_TWINS=0.34.0
MOCKS_BUNDLE_TWINS=0.10.2
# Toolchain floors the workflows select and the trees declare.
XCODE=26.6
JDK=25
GRADLE=9.7.1
GRADLE_SHA256=acd53f1edaf02f1a8ff99879f8a34b302661a057d9b063ae9e35b552f804d20a
KOTLIN=2.4.10
